{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>Why should I be bereft even of you two in one day.</b> Your father and you — since Esau said, 'the days of mourning for my father draw near,' etc. — it follows that Isaac dies, Esau kills Jacob, and then I would be bereft of both of them in one day — of my husband and of my son. And the primary interpretation is as Rashi explained. And <b>gam</b> comes to include Rebekah, to say: when she is bereft of her sons, she is accounted as dead." "<b>In one day.</b> Even though their deaths did not occur on one day, their burial at any rate was on one day. Thus it is taught in tractate Sotah."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:23.901885840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}